uctions:\n\nExtract the food item(s) from the user's query.\n\nFor each item, provide the nutritional content (Calories, Protein, Carbs, and Fat) for a standard serving size.\n\nIf a serving size is specified in the query (e.g., \"1 cup of rice\"), use that. Otherwise, use a common standard serving size.\n\n\nOutput Format: return JSON by default, but also add a text summary field inside the response. Example:\n{\n  \"foods_items\": [\n    {\"name\":\"amala\",\"calories\":112,\"protein\":2,\"carbs\":27,\"fat\":0.2},\n    {\"name\":\"ewedu\",\"calories\":35,\"protein\":2,\"carbs\":5,\"fat\":0},\n    {\"name\":\"goat meat\",\"calories\":143,\"protein\":27,\"carbs\":0,\"fat\":3}\n  ],\n  \"total\": {\"calories\":290,\"protein\":31,\"carbs\":32,\"fat\":3.2},\n  \"summary\": \"Amala (112 cal), Ewedu (35 cal), Goat Meat (143 cal) → Total: 290 cal\"\n}\n\nAdditional Guidance: If the food item is not in your knowledge base, respond by saying you could not find the information and suggest the user try a different query.\n\n\n=====================\n\n\nFrom the provided text or image, identify ONLY the names of the food items. \n\nReturn your answer as ONLY a simple JSON array of the names. For example: [\"food one\", \"food two\"].\n\nDo not include serving sizes, calories, protein, carbs, fat, or any other nutritional information. ","options":{}},"type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent","typeVersion":2.2,"position":[352,-64],"id":"5ef9bdd9-ee49-4c2b-98c7-0b97bc7b6882","name":"Food Detection AI: Text"},{"parameters":{"documentId":{"__rl":true,"value":"1p1wZqfDipZtKbzpax_ro8nJPNrN5OaXOLuYoiENrQXk","mode":"list","cachedResultName":"FoodDictionaryTemplate (Cal AI)","cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1p1wZqfDipZtKbzpax_ro8nJPNrN5OaXOLuYoiENrQXk/edit?usp=drivesdk"},"sheetName":{"__rl":true,"value":109632443,"mode":"list","cachedResultName":"Approved Foods","cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1p1wZqfDipZtKbzpax_ro8nJPNrN5OaXOLuYoiENrQXk/